    <bpmn:process id="W_W961" name="W961. BSP Anti-Money Laundering (AML) Covered Transaction Reporting" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Cash transaction at POS exceeds PHP 500,000 single transaction threshold, or aggregate cash transactions from same customer exceed PHP 500,000 in a 5-business-day rolling period (internal conservative trigger; the statutory test is one banking day), or suspicious transaction indicators detected
Frequency: ~50–100 covered transactions/month chain-wide
Volume: 1 covered transaction report (CTR) per triggering event
Owner: Compliance Officer
Participants: Cashier, Store Manager, Compliance Officer, BSA/AML Analyst, Anti-Money Laundering Council (AMLC), Finance
Source: workflow W961 — BSP Anti-Money Laundering (AML) Covered Transaction Reporting</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W961_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W961_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W961_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W961_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W961_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W961_Lane2" name="Compliance Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W961_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W961_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W961_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W961_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W961_Start4" name="Cash transaction at POS exceeds PHP 500,000 single transaction threshold, or aggregate…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W961_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W961_Task5" name="Transaction Monitoring &amp; Threshold Detection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Transaction Monitoring &amp; Threshold Detection: (a) system monitors all cash transactions in real-time per W533: (i) single cash transaction ≥ PHP 500,000 → immediate CTR trigger; (ii) aggregate cash transactions per customer (matched by loyalty ID, customer account, or cashier-entered name/mobile) ≥ PHP 500,000 within 5-business-day rolling window → CTR trigger; (iii) system flags: customer identity (name, ID type/number, address, nationality, date of birth, contact number from loyalty profile or cashier entry), transaction details (amount, date, time, store, items purchased, POS terminal ID); (b) Cashier procedure for large cash transactions: (i) for transactions ≥ PHP 500,000 cash: Cashier must request and record valid government ID per W530 high-value transaction documentation; (ii) ID details entered into POS before transaction completion; (iii) Cashier does NOT inform customer that transaction is being reported to AMLC (tipping off is a criminal offense per AMLA)
Responsible (R): System / Cashier
Accountable (A): Compliance Officer
Duration: 5–10 min (Cashier ID verification)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W961_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W961_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W961_Task6" name="Suspicious Transaction Indicator Detection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Suspicious Transaction Indicator Detection: System and Cashier monitor for red flags regardless of amount: (a) system-detected: (i) multiple cash transactions just below PHP 500,000 threshold by same customer in short period (structuring); (ii) customer frequently purchases high-value items with cash and returns them for store credit (placement-layering); (iii) cash purchases by customers flagged on sanction/PEP lists per W730; (iv) unusual purchasing patterns (large volume of easily resellable items — power tools, appliances); (b) Cashier-observed: (i) customer appears nervous or evasive about providing ID; (ii) customer accompanied by multiple individuals each making separate cash payments; (iii) cash appears unusual (brand new bills, sequential serial numbers); (iv) customer insists on paying cash despite having credit card; (c) flagged transactions routed to Compliance Officer for STR assessment
Responsible (R): System / Cashier
Accountable (A): Compliance Officer
Duration: 5–10 min (Cashier observation)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W961_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W961_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W961_Task7" name="CTR/STR Preparation &amp; Filing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: CTR/STR Preparation &amp; Filing: Compliance Officer prepares and files: (a) Covered Transaction Report (CTR): (i) filed via AMLC online portal within 5 business days of transaction; (ii) includes: customer identification, transaction details, store location, purpose of transaction (as stated by customer); (iii) supporting documents: POS transaction record, customer ID copy, CCTV footage reference per W838; (b) Suspicious Transaction Report (STR): (i) filed via AMLC portal within 5 business days of determination that transaction is suspicious; (ii) includes: all CTR data plus suspicious indicators, Cashier observations, and Compliance Officer assessment; (iii) STR filed EVEN IF transaction is below PHP 500,000 threshold; (c) AMLC acknowledgment receipt stored in compliance document repository per W255 with 5-year retention
Responsible (R): Compliance Officer / BSA-AML Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: 30–60 min/report</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W961_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W961_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W961_Task8" name="Record Retention &amp; Audit Trail">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Record Retention &amp; Audit Trail: (a) all CTR/STR-related documents retained for 5 years per AMLA: (i) POS transaction details; (ii) customer ID copies (secure storage per RA 10173); (iii) AMLC acknowledgment receipts; (iv) internal assessment notes; (v) CCTV footage for transaction period; (b) system maintains audit trail: who prepared, who reviewed, when filed, AMLC receipt number; (c) Internal Audit includes AML compliance in annual audit plan per W354 AML screening audit
Responsible (R): Compliance Officer / IT
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W961_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W961_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W961_Task9" name="Quarterly AML Program Review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly AML Program Review: (a) Compliance Officer reviews: (i) CTR filing volume and timeliness; (ii) STR filing volume and outcomes; (iii) false positive rate (transactions flagged but determined non-suspicious); (iv) Cashier AML awareness metrics per W730 training program; (v) any AMLC inquiries or investigations; (b) annual: Compliance Officer updates AML risk assessment for BuildRight&#x27;s business model; (c) annual: Cashier AML training refresher per W730 program
Responsible (R): Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance / CEO
Duration: 4–6 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W961_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W961_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W961_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W961_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W961_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-308 (ensure controlled execution — Government Audit &amp; Inspection Response (PA-22.2).)
Owner: Compliance Officer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
