    <bpmn:process id="W_W1404" name="W1404. DENR Environmental Compliance Inspection Response, Documentation Package &amp; Corrective Action Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: DENR regional or local inspection notice; or unannounced DENR inspection at store/DC/HQ location
Frequency: Periodic (~10–20 inspections/year chain-wide (per the Volume register)); higher frequency for DCs with hazardous material storage and stores with DENR Permit to Operate (W477)
Volume: ~10–20 DENR inspections/year chain-wide; primarily targeting DCs (4) and stores with significant paint/chemical departments
Owner: Compliance Officer
Participants: Compliance Officer, Store/DC Manager, Facilities Coordinator, Environmental Consultant, VP Legal, DENR Inspector
Source: workflow W1404 — DENR Environmental Compliance Inspection Response, Documentation Package &amp; Corrective Action Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1404_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1404_Lane1" name="Compliance Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1404_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1404_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1404_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1404_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1404_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1404_Lane2" name="Store">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1404_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1404_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1404_Lane3" name="DENR Inspector">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1404_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1404_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1404_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1404_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1404_Start5" name="DENR regional or local inspection notice; or unannounced DENR inspection at store/DC/HQ…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1404_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1404_Task6" name="Pre-inspection preparedness">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Pre-inspection preparedness: Compliance Officer maintains DENR inspection readiness kit per location: (a) current PTO and WDP displayed in accessible location, (b) Material Safety Data Sheets (MSDS/SDS) binder for all hazardous materials stocked at the location, (c) hazardous waste disposal manifests (per W82) for the last 2 years, (d) Self-Monitoring Report (SMR) and Compliance Monitoring Report (CMR) submission records (per W433), (e) emergency response plan for chemical spills (per W1312), (f) employee training records for hazmat handling (per W24.3)
Responsible (R): Compliance Officer / Store Manager
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Quarterly review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1404_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1404_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1404_Task7" name="Inspection day — announced">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Inspection day — announced: DENR inspector arrives; Store/DC Manager greets and escorts; Compliance Officer (or Facilities Coordinator for remote locations) participates as BuildRight representative; inspector presents credentials and states scope of inspection (air quality, wastewater, hazardous waste storage, PTO compliance, general environmental management)
Responsible (R): Store/DC Manager / Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Full day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1404_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1404_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1404_Task8" name="Inspection day — unannounced">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Inspection day — unannounced: DENR inspector arrives without prior notice; Store/DC Manager receives inspector, verifies DENR credentials, and contacts Compliance Officer immediately; Compliance Officer provides phone guidance while traveling to site if feasible; Store Manager provides access to all requested areas and documents per legal obligation
Responsible (R): Store/DC Manager / Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Full day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1404_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1404_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1404_Task9" name="Inspector tours facility: (a) hazardous material storage area (paint/chemical…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Inspector tours facility: (a) hazardous material storage area (paint/chemical section, garden chemicals, cement storage) — checks proper labeling, ventilation, secondary containment, fire suppression, SDS accessibility; (b) wastewater discharge point — checks effluent quality visually, reviews wastewater treatment if applicable; (c) hazardous waste storage area — checks proper segregation, labeling, storage duration (must not exceed the 90-day on-site accumulation limit per DENR DAO 2013-22), disposal manifest completeness; (d) general housekeeping and spill containment equipment; (e) air emission points if applicable (generator exhaust per W808)
Responsible (R): DENR Inspector / Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 3–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1404_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1404_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1404_Task10" name="Inspector reviews documentation: PTO validity, WDP compliance, SMR/CMR filing…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Inspector reviews documentation: PTO validity, WDP compliance, SMR/CMR filing history, hazardous waste disposal manifests and transporter licenses (per W82), hazardous waste generator registration, employee training records, incident logs for spills or releases
Responsible (R): DENR Inspector / Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1404_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1404_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1404_Task11" name="Inspector conducts exit interview: verbally communicates initial findings and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Inspector conducts exit interview: verbally communicates initial findings and any observed violations; provides written inspection report (if issued on-site) or states that formal report will follow within 15–30 days; Store Manager signs acknowledgment of inspection (not admission of violation)
Responsible (R): DENR Inspector / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Compliance Officer
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1404_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1404_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1404_Task12" name="If no violations found">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: If no violations found: Compliance Officer files inspection record with clean report; location continues normal operations; inspection record stored in DENR compliance archive for 5 years
Responsible (R): Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1404_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1404_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1404_Task13" name="If violations observed">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: If violations observed: Compliance Officer initiates corrective action process: (a) document each cited violation with specific DENR regulation reference, (b) assess severity (minor administrative vs. substantive environmental risk), (c) engage Environmental Consultant for corrective action plan development if substantive, (d) develop corrective action plan with timeline and responsible person per violation, (e) submit corrective action plan to DENR within prescribed period (typically 15–30 days from notice of violation), (f) implement corrective actions, (g) schedule DENR re-inspection to verify compliance, (h) pay assessed fines if applicable (contested or accepted per Legal advice)
Responsible (R): Compliance Officer / Environmental Consultant
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: 1–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1404_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1404_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1404_Task14" name="Quarterly: Compliance Officer reviews all DENR inspection results and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Quarterly: Compliance Officer reviews all DENR inspection results and corrective action statuses; generates DENR compliance dashboard: inspections completed, violations by type, corrective action closure rate, outstanding fines, locations with chronic issues; escalates chronic non-compliance locations to VP Legal &amp; Compliance and COO
Responsible (R): Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: 2 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1404_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1404_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1404_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1404_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1404_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-308 (ensure controlled execution — Government Audit &amp; Inspection Response (PA-22.2).) | - operational: documentation
Owner: Compliance Officer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1404_Assoc17" sourceRef="W1404_Annotation16" targetRef="W1404_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
